(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2608301615-mail-a2a-binding")
  (:adr/title "MailA2A: email, x402, and MLS as an A2A store-and-forward binding")
  (:adr/status :accepted)
  (:adr/date "2026-08-30")
  (:adr/source-format "edn")
  (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/mail-a2a :protocol/a2a :protocol/email :protocol/x402 :protocol/mls))
  (:adr/body "# ADR-2608301615: MailA2A — email, x402, and MLS as an A2A store-and-forward binding\n\n## Context\n\nThe workspace already has the components but not their common wire contract. `kotoba-lang/mail` is the portable mail model; `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-mime` parses RFC 5322/MIME; `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-mls` implements RFC 9420 primitives; Cloud Itonami has an HTTP A2A adapter; and `network-awai/nexus-x402` has HTTP-oriented x402 facilities.\n\nExternal standards leave a gap rather than an absence of precedent. FIPA explicitly used SMTP addresses as agent transport examples, ECMA-430 defines NLIP, A2A v1.0 defines the current task/data model and permits custom bindings, x402 v2 makes its objects transport-neutral, and MIME/S/MIME/OpenPGP/MLS provide packaging and cryptography. None combines current A2A operations, email correlation, x402 v2, end-to-end email security, and MLS group state in one email binding.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `kotoba-lang/mail-a2a` as the experimental **MailA2A Binding 1.0** and portable reference validator. It is a subject-plane reusable protocol, not an actor or mail service.\n\n1. **A2A remains the semantic model.** Each email is one request, response, error, or ordered event. The protected `application/a2a+json` part carries canonical A2A v1.0 payloads. SMTP acceptance, DSNs, and mailbox flags are never task completion.\n2. **RFC 5322 supplies store-and-forward correlation.** `Message-ID`, `In-Reply-To`, and `References` describe the mail thread. Protected message/correlation/task/context IDs remain authoritative. Experimental `Mail-A2A-*` fields are routing hints only.\n3. **Email streaming is a sequence, not SSE.** Gaps pause delivery and recover through buffering or `tasks/get`; terminal task states require a final event. Idempotency, expiry, duplicate bytes, conflicting IDs, and replay tuples are explicit.\n4. **x402 objects are unchanged.** A MailA2A wrapper declares v2 and carries exact `PaymentRequired`, `PaymentPayload`, or `SettlementResponse`. HTTP 402 and `PAYMENT-*` headers are not copied into email. Wallet keys never enter a mailbox or relay.\n5. **Direct-message security reuses S/MIME 4.0, OpenPGP/MIME, or a declared detached-JWS profile.** SMTP TLS and DKIM/DMARC are transport/domain signals, not agent authorization. Security-relevant values stay inside authenticated content; RFC 9787/9788 header protection is recommended.\n6. **Private groups use RFC 9420 MLS.** The protected envelope is MLS application data in `message/mls`; a list distributes identical opaque bytes. Membership changes only through MLS state. Static recipient fan-out is not called MLS.\n7. **Human fallback has no authority.** `text/plain` may explain a message but cannot extend or override protected A2A data.\n\n## Publication and implementation\n\n- Source: <https://github.com/kotoba-lang/mail-a2a>\n- Binding URI: <https://kotoba-lang.github.io/mail-a2a/spec/v1/>\n- Upstream proposal: <https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/issues/2191>\n- Child main commit: `3a1a2347330bf4b16977278105039cbd591a3f2a` (PR #1 links the proposal; protocol semantics are in initial commit `7a54aedf0cf51b86aa051c2cd4a959daa097c98e`).\n- Published artifacts: normative spec, JSON Schema, Agent Card and EML examples, security policy, and a portable `.cljc` envelope/event-order validator.\n- `manifest/repos.edn` and the generated single `mail-a2a` block in `manifest/west.yml` register the child.\n\n## Verification\n\n- JVM: 8 tests / 16 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- ClojureScript via nbb: 8 tests / 16 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- JSON Schema and Agent Card parse; both EML examples parse and contain `application/a2a+json`.\n- New-JVM-surface policy self-test passes; production source is `.cljc`, no production `.clj`.\n- GitHub Pages root and binding URI both returned HTTP 200 after build.\n- West orphan audit reports no blocking registration gap; generated-manifest check is canonical; child HEAD equals the single west revision.\n\n## Qualification boundary\n\nThis proves a designed, implemented, tested, and publicly published **community binding and validator**, plus an upstream proposal. It does not prove A2A maintainer sponsorship or adoption, IANA registration of experimental mail fields, live SMTP/IMAP interoperability, real S/MIME/OpenPGP/MLS exchange, real x402 verification/settlement, or bot-to-bot production traffic. Those require separate governance and live evidence.\n\n## References\n\nA2A v1.0 and Custom Protocol Binding guidance; x402 v2; ECMA-430–434; FIPA Abstract Architecture and Agent Message Transport Service; RFC 5322, RFC 2045–2049, RFC 2392, RFC 8551, RFC 9580, RFC 3156, RFC 9787, RFC 9788, and RFC 9420.")))
